ng element in the returned array. A thread is alive if it has\n-            // been started and has not yet died.\n+\n+        // NOTE, javadoc of getThreadInfo says: If a thread of the given ID is not alive or does not exist,\n+        // null will be set in the corresponding element in the returned array. A thread is alive if it has\n+        // been started and has not yet died.\n+        for (int j \u003d 0; j \u003c threadElementsSnapshotCount - 1; j++) {\n             result[j] \u003d threadBean.getThreadInfo(threadIds, Integer.MAX_VALUE);\n             Thread.sleep(threadElementsSnapshotDelay.millis());\n         }\n+        result[threadElementsSnapshotCount - 1] \u003d threadBean.getThreadInfo(threadIds, Integer.MAX_VALUE);","submitted_line":288},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The change in `captureThreadStacks` modifies the loop to iterate one less time and then makes a final call outside the loop. This could lead to inconsistent behavior if `threadElementsSnapshotCount` is 1, as it would skip capturing thread stacks entirely. Ensure that this logic aligns with the intended behavior.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/monitor/jvm/HotThreads.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/monitor/jvm/HotThreads.java-10358:10395,11877:11914-11969:11990,13258:13277,13480:13512,19936:19955","promptId":"#K06WJ","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/monitor/jvm/HotThreads.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/monitor/jvm/HotThreads.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":10358,"endPos":10395,"startLine":273,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":273,"endLineOffset":45,"length":38},{"pos":11877,"endPos":11914,"startLine":302,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":302,"endLineOffset":45,"length":38}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":11969,"endPos":11990,"startLine":304,"startLineOffset":112,"endLine":304,"endLineOffset":133,"length":22},{"pos":13258,"endPos":13277,"startLine":329,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":329,"endLineOffset":27,"length":20},{"pos":1